From: Hummingbird RPM maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] livestore: treat canceled initial offset fetch as stop

Shutdown may cancel the partition reader before its initial Kafka offset
lookup completes. Match the later polling path by treating cancellation as a
clean stop instead of failing the service. This behavior is present in Tempo
3.0 and is backported here for the 2.10 stream.

diff --git a/modules/livestore/partition_reader.go b/modules/livestore/partition_reader.go
--- a/modules/livestore/partition_reader.go
+++ b/modules/livestore/partition_reader.go
@@ -82,5 +82,10 @@ func (r *PartitionReader) running(ctx context.Context) error {
 	offset, err := r.fetchLastCommittedOffsetWithRetries(ctx)
 	if err != nil {
+		// Shutdown can cancel the reader before the initial offset lookup completes.
+		// Treat that as a clean stop instead of failing the service.
+		if ctx.Err() != nil {
+			return nil
+		}
 		return fmt.Errorf("failed to fetch last committed offset: %w", err)
 	}
 
